From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:51:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 17/40] Compressed operator: one operator index per z-vector

Operator_SSE_Compressed allocated m_Op_index per cell (NX x NY x NZ 32-bit entries), although the operator
and the engines only use the entries of the z-vectors (zv < numVectors). On meshes of up to 42 z lines
every 128-byte cache line of the array holds used entries, so the engines streamed 4 B of index per cell
instead of 1 B. The index is now allocated per z-vector; OPENEMS_OP_INDEX_PER_CELL=1 keeps the old
allocation. The values are the same, only the array is smaller (bit-identical).

Paired interleaved A/B, multithreaded engine, 5 rounds, other processes on 0.4-1.7 cores: patch x5 x1.119
at 4 threads and x1.101 at 8, notch x3 x1.042 and x1.052, the GCPW line, the SMA launch and the two
tutorials x1.005-x1.021. Memory: about 3 B per cell less (notch x3 15.8 MB, patch x5 23.6 MB).

Generated-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
Signed-off-by: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 FDTD/operator_sse_compressed.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/FDTD/operator_sse_compressed.cpp b/FDTD/operator_sse_compressed.cpp
index 984dae6..8684703 100644
--- a/FDTD/operator_sse_compressed.cpp
+++ b/FDTD/operator_sse_compressed.cpp
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 #include <iostream>
 #include "engine_sse_compressed.h"
 #include "engine_sse.h"
+#include "tools/useful.h"
 
 #include <map>
 #include <cstring>
@@ -100,7 +101,13 @@ void Operator_SSE_Compressed::InitOperator()
 	}
 
 	Operator_sse::InitOperator();
-	m_Op_index.Init("Op_index", numLines);
+	// one index per f4vector (x, y, zv): the operator and the engines use zv < numVectors only, and with numLines[2]
+	// entries per (x, y) the unused ones shared the cache lines of the used ones on meshes of up to 42 z lines, so the
+	// engines streamed 4 B of index per cell instead of 1 B (OPENEMS_OP_INDEX_PER_CELL=1: the old layout, to compare)
+	if (EnvFlag("OPENEMS_OP_INDEX_PER_CELL"))
+		m_Op_index.Init("Op_index", numLines);
+	else
+		m_Op_index.Init("Op_index", {numLines[0], numLines[1], numVectors});
 }
 
